From d418103efd12630a1270d43a8fcb814c90c181e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:12:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH BlueZ 1/2] shared/mgmt: Fix notify leak in mgmt_unregister()

mgmt_unregister() called from a notification callback takes the entry
off notify_list and only marks it removed. process_notify() frees the
removed entries still on notify_list once the walk is done, so this
one is never freed and its destroy callback never runs.

If the callback unregisters the next entry rather than its own, this
is also a use-after-free: queue_foreach() has already saved that
entry's queue node, and queue_remove_if() frees it. This is the crash
that commit 872729a91632 ("shared/mgmt: Fix crash when removing
index") fixed for mgmt_unregister_index(), still present in
mgmt_unregister().

Leave the entry on the list while notifying, as
mgmt_unregister_index() and mgmt_unregister_all() do, and let
process_notify() free it. An entry already marked removed is no
longer registered, so unregistering it returns false. For an entry
marked by mgmt_unregister_index() or mgmt_unregister_all() it used to
return true, take the entry off the list and leak it.

mgmt-tester, mesh-tester and userchan-tester unregister from event
callbacks, and under ASan each reports these entries as leaked, for
example userchan-tester:

  Direct leak of 80 byte(s) in 2 object(s) allocated from:
    #0 in malloc
    #1 in util_malloc src/shared/util.c:46
    #2 in mgmt_register src/shared/mgmt.c:974
    #3 in test_open_success tools/userchan-tester.c:275

Fixes: 872729a91632 ("shared/mgmt: Fix crash when removing index")
---
 src/shared/mgmt.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shared/mgmt.c b/src/shared/mgmt.c
index f56bcee14..f5aeecf3f 100644
--- a/src/shared/mgmt.c
+++ b/src/shared/mgmt.c
@@ -999,18 +999,28 @@ bool mgmt_unregister(struct mgmt *mgmt, unsigned int id)
 	if (!mgmt || !id)
 		return false;
 
-	notify = queue_remove_if(mgmt->notify_list, match_notify_id,
+	/*
+	 * While notifying, leave the entry on the list for process_notify()
+	 * to free once it is done with it.
+	 */
+	if (mgmt->in_notify) {
+		notify = queue_find(mgmt->notify_list, match_notify_id,
 							UINT_TO_PTR(id));
-	if (!notify)
-		return false;
+		if (!notify || notify->removed)
+			return false;
+
+		notify->removed = true;
+		mgmt->need_notify_cleanup = true;
 
-	if (!mgmt->in_notify) {
-		destroy_notify(notify);
 		return true;
 	}
 
-	notify->removed = true;
-	mgmt->need_notify_cleanup = true;
+	notify = queue_remove_if(mgmt->notify_list, match_notify_id,
+							UINT_TO_PTR(id));
+	if (!notify)
+		return false;
+
+	destroy_notify(notify);
 
 	return true;
 }

